  "text": "With ten seeds per rank the rank sweep is completely sign-separated: every run at r=3,4,5 is negative and every run at r=6,7,8 is positive, so the crossing lies between r=5 and r=6. Of the 15 rank pairs, 14 separate under an exact two-sided permutation test over all 184756 splits of the 20 pooled runs (raw p<0.05, unchanged by Holm-Bonferroni across the 15 tests); the single exception is the adjacent pair r=7 vs r=8 (difference +40.0, exact p=0.0709), for which the percentile bootstrap CI [-77.20, -0.25] happens to exclude zero by +0.25 energy units -- the exact test governs and this pair is reported as unresolved. Adjacent-rank differences are resolved for r=3 vs r=4 (p=0.0100), r=4 vs r=5 (p=0.00235), r=5 vs r=6 (p=1.08e-5) and r=6 vs r=7 (p=1.08e-5), but not for r=7 vs r=8. The same ten seed labels appear in every rank, so we also ran the exact paired sign-flip test over the 1024 sign patterns of the ten paired differences: it reaches its minimum attainable p=2/1024=0.0020 for twelve pairs and likewise leaves r=7 vs r=8 unresolved (p=0.0605). The frequently quoted p=2/C(20,10)=1.1e-5 for r=5 vs r=6 is confirmed exactly (previously unarchived); the archived r=3 vs r=8 value 1.0825e-5 is reproduced to machine precision. For the near-zero rank r=5 the equivalence test against zero fails at the pre-declared one-seed-sd margin (38.77): TOST p=0.652, and equivalence would need a margin of +66.2 (1.71 seed sd); the ten-seed r=5 group is therefore not statistically indistinguishable from zero, only the smallest-magnitude negative rank. For the VQA-RAD claim, token F1 shows no rank ordering (r=5 minus r=6 = +0.0067, TOST p=0.0074 within +/-0.05) while exact-match accuracy shows a small reversal (+0.0433, 95% CI [+0.0033, +0.0833]); the accuracy ordering can only be excluded above a margin of 0.0767."
